Since this is a detailed, specific Thanksgiving plan with particular timing constraints (one oven, specific dish sequences, 8 people, finish at 18:00), I'll build the program from the source text.

**Analysis of the workflow:**

- **Turkey** is the anchor: 40 min rest before, 20 min preheat, 20 min prep, 180 min roast, 40 min rest = ~380 min total to "ready to carve"
- **Gravy** starts when turkey comes out (3 steps: drippings → flour → stock/simmer)
- **Stuffing** prep happens early (bread cubing), veg sauté 20 min before turkey out, assembly 10 min, then bake 35 min starting when turkey exits
- **Green beans**: start 10 min after turkey out (blanch, make sauce, combine, bake 20 min after stuffing exits)
- **Potatoes**: start when turkey out (peel/quarter, boil, mash, hold warm)
- **Rolls**: warm 8 min after casserole exits
- **Serve**: when all ready

Working backward from 18:00:
- Carving: 15 min → done by 17:45, start at 17:30
- Turkey rest: 40 min → start at 16:50
- Turkey roast: 180 min → start at 13:30
- Turkey preheat: 20 min → start at 13:10
- Turkey rest before: 40 min → start at 12:30

This means we need to start at approximately 12:30 to finish by 18:00.

